// Intune policy deleted or reassigned
//
// Fires when an Intune policy gets deleted or its assignment changes. Deleting or
// unassigning an AV or ASR policy is one of the quietest ways to weaken every device at
// once.
//
// Runs:      Every hour
// Severity:  Low
// MITRE:     T1562.001
// Tables:    IntuneAuditLogs (Sentinel)
// Custom details: Actor, Target
//
// Needs:
//   - Intune diagnostic settings sending audit logs to your Sentinel workspace, with the
//     workspace connected to the Defender portal.
//   - Microsoft Sentinel Contributor to create it.
//   - Map the account entity to the Actor column yourself. Sentinel data doesn't map on
//     its own.
//
// Triage (paste into Recommended actions):
//   - Check if it's an AV, ASR, EDR, firewall or baseline policy, and if there's a ticket.
//   - Escalate if a security policy got deleted or unassigned with no ticket.
//   - Close if it's a ticketed change.

IntuneAuditLogs
| where OperationName contains "Delete" or OperationName contains "Assign"
| extend Props = parse_json(Properties)
| extend Actor = coalesce(tostring(Props.Actor.UPN), Identity), Target = tostring(Props.TargetDisplayNames[0])
| project TimeGenerated, Actor, OperationName, Category, Target, ResultType, CorrelationId
